    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.deps\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nhttps://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/6bf9eccaf2a5395b254bc031f9812cf163ca4187/scripts/init-deps-example.lua#L45\nTreesitter devs say that it doesn't support lazy loading (both old \"master\" and new \"main\" branch versions):\nhttps://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter/tree/main?tab=readme-ov-file#installation\nhttps://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter?tab=readme-ov-file#installation\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. \n```\nls ~/.config/nvim-repro/\nexample.rs  init.lua\n```\n\n2. init.lua:\n```lua\n-- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\nlocal clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim', mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\nrequire('mini.deps').setup()\n\n-- REPRO\n-- it was yanked from my main config as is\nMiniDeps.later(function()\n    MiniDeps.add({\n        source = 'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter',\n        checkout = 'main',\n        hooks = { post_checkout = function() vim.cmd('TSUpdate') end },\n    })\n    -- in my main config i do \"install({ 'all' })\"\n    require('nvim-treesitter').install({ 'rust' })\n    local langs = require('nvim-treesitter').get_installed()\n    vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('FileType', {\n        pattern = langs,\n        callback = function()\n            vim.treesitter.start(); vim.bo.indentexpr = \"v:lua.require'nvim-treesitter'.indentexpr()\"\n            -- the indentexpr stuff is not related to the issue\n        end,\n    })\nend)\n```\n3. example.rs:\n```rust\nfn main() {\n    println!(\"mini\");\n}\n```\n\n4. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim example.rs` and see `println!` doesn't get highlighted unless explicitly called `:lua vim.treesitter.start()` inside neovim.\n\n5. Change init.lua to use `MiniDeps.now()` and treesitter loads as expected.",
